  "Question": "Kate rode her bicycle for \\(30\\) minutes at a speed of \\(16\\) mph, then walked for \\(90\\) minutes at a speed of \\(4\\) mph. What was her overall average speed in miles per hour?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(12\\)",
    "E": "\\(14\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Overall average speed is total distance divided by total time, so first find the distance for each part of the trip. The times are \\(30\\) minutes \\(=\\tfrac12\\) hour and \\(90\\) minutes \\(=\\tfrac32\\) hours. Thus Kate rides \\(16\\cdot\\tfrac12=8\\) miles and walks \\(4\\cdot\\tfrac32=6\\) miles. Her average speed is\n\\[\n\\frac{8+6}{\\tfrac12+\\tfrac32}\n=\\frac{14}{2}=7\\text{ mph}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice A.",
